      "hints": [
        "For a spring in its proportional region, the spring constant is the gradient of a force–extension graph.",
        "Choose a clear point on the line, convert its extension from centimetres to metres, then calculate F / x."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Use Hooke's law F = kx, so k = F / x; this is also the gradient of the force–extension graph.",
        "A clear point on the line is F = 7.0 N at x = 5.0 cm = 5.0 × 10⁻² m.",
        "k = 7.0 / (5.0 × 10⁻²) = 140 N m⁻¹."
      ],
      "checking": {
