      "hints": [
        "The elastic potential energy is the area under the force–extension graph up to the stated extension.",
        "At 4.0 cm, use the graph force and the triangular area ½Fx, after converting the extension to metres."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "For a spring in the proportional region, elastic potential energy is the area under its force–extension graph: Eₚ = ½Fx = ½kx².",
        "At x = 4.0 cm = 4.0 × 10⁻² m, the graph gives F = 5.6 N.",
        "Eₚ = ½ × 5.6 × 4.0 × 10⁻² = 0.112 J, which rounds to 0.11 J."
      ],
